{
  "id": "pokemon-daisuki-club",
  "name": "Pokémon Daisuki Club",
  "category": "program",
  "description": {
    "text": "The Pokémon Daisuki Club (ポケモン大好きクラブ), started in late January 2004, was the official fan club for every side of Pokémon. Its website ran the Pokémon Card Game First Classroom (はじめて教室), a course with the teacher Okajii on the rules, battle tactics and deckbuilding: those who answered all eight quizzes correctly between 1 July and 1 August 2005 entered a draw for 10,000 copies of Pokémon Fan Club, which carries the club's name and logo.\n\nWhen three of the five Battle Road Spring 2008 tournaments were canceled, its promos Magnezone, Dusknoir and Pikachu were sent from 1 July 2008, with the club card, to everyone who had applied for the free Pokémon Daisuki Club Card by 2 June 2008. That summer members could also collect the 13 Collection Challenge cards in a mini-game on the club's website until 1 September 2008, and 300 of those who collected nine won, by draw, a set of the twelve cards given out at shops and events. The club's PCG Action Points prizes are under Pokémon Daisuki Club Action Points.",
